title: Use `OnChainContext` for `check_inherents`
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    `sp_block_builder::check_inherents` and `sp_block_builder::check_inherents_with_data` now call
    the `check_inherents` runtime API with `CallContext::Onchain { import: true }`. The extrinsics of
    the block to check could already have been built by a new runtime, so they need to be checked
    with the on-chain runtime as well. Before checking the inherents, `initialize_block` is now
    called on the same runtime api instance, so that pending runtime migrations are applied before
    the new runtime checks the inherents. This affects all import queues using these functions
    (Aura, BABE, PoW and the Cumulus import queues).
crates:
- name: sp-block-builder
  bump: patch
